  "Comment": {
    "type": "cexostring",
    "value": "Dwarven Defender initiation reward (roadmap: dwarven-defender-quest), given by q_dwd_finish with 1000 XP when the Shard of the Unbroken Stone is handed to Halmir. Mirrors the sibling prestige rewards' power tier (three +3-tier properties, no AB/damage -- forge-cap-safe), themed for the last hold of Khazad: Craft Armor +3 (skill subtype 25, SKILL_CRAFT_ARMOR), Taunt +3 (skill subtype 18, SKILL_TAUNT -- the defender draws the blows), Saving Throw Bonus vs Sonic +3 (IP_CONST_SAVEVS_SONIC = 15, verified in ovr/nwscript.nss -- the drums in the deep; no vs-traps save constant exists). Deliberately avoids all sibling reward skills (Heal/Persuade on the DivCh mantle, Discipline/Parry on the WM buckle, etc.). BaseItem 17 (helmet) + ModelPart1 17 + colors copied from the module's existing Helm of The Defender (012)."
  },
  "Cost": {
    "type": "dword",
    "value": 0
  },
  "Cursed": {
    "type": "byte",
    "value": 0
  },
  "DescIdentified": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "A dwarf-forged warhelm of grey steel, unadorned but for a single band of granite set above the brow -- cut, the smiths say, from stone that would not break. The Defenders of Khazad-dum wore its like on the doors and bridges of the deep places, where the line is the wall and the wall does not step back. Halmir the Grey gave it over when the Shard of the Unbroken Stone was laid in his hand -- the token of those the orders call Dwarven Defenders, whose page is cut deep in his roll, the way Durin's folk cut what they mean to keep."
    }
  },
